      "writtenOn": "2017-04-05T22:11:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree. If the user has a default project and a role assignment on that project they will get a project-scoped token even if they authenticate without scope in the request. If that is the case, they must provide a \"unscoped\" in the scope request in order to get an unscoped token.\n\nWe need to omit the ambiguity in this statement. Doing so will be helpful since this behavior has caused confusion before.",
